 ## Overview
-Lookup Table and Configuration provides the static data structures and mapping logic that determine how a voxel's scalar field sign configuration is converted into mesh geometry. It solves the combinatorial problem of isosurface extraction by replacing runtime conditional branching with direct array indexing, enabling $O(1)$ determination of triangle topology per voxel. It differs from symmetry-based approaches by handling all 256 cases explicitly (or via symmetry reduction) and from dynamic ambiguity resolution methods by using fixed triangulations for ambiguous cases, which may produce topological artifacts if adjacent cells resolve ambiguities inconsistently.
+Lookup Table and Configuration provides the static data structures and mapping logic that determine how a voxel's scalar field sign configuration is converted into mesh geometry [G]. It solves the combinatorial problem of isosurface extraction by replacing runtime conditional branching with direct array indexing, enabling $O(1)$ determination of triangle topology per voxel [G]. It differs from symmetry-based approaches by handling all 256 cases explicitly (or via symmetry reduction) and from dynamic ambiguity resolution methods by using fixed triangulations for ambiguous cases, which may produce topological artifacts if adjacent cells resolve ambiguities inconsistently [G].
 
